  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nThis is a scoped structural result: **no new \u03ba, no construction.** It adds only `research/complex-rank8-rigidity-p110-odd/`. The selected record, `upstream/` and all frozen pins are unchanged.\n\n#1419 shows that rank-8 rigidity of #1212's system (E) passes to supersets. That makes P112 minus any **orthogonal** pair rigid. It cannot reach an **odd pair**, because no frame contains one. The 2912 odd pairs of P112 form two FRAME0-stabiliser orbits, of sizes 224 and 2688. This PR proves rigidity on both, by #1212's method plus #1399's Lemma 9. For each orbit representative it ships a pivot and a new zero-exclusion certificate.\n\n- **Inputs, per representative:**\n  - (I2) zero exclusion: a DRUP refutation, of 1893 and 2320 lemmas, of #1212's zero-pattern CNF families (two/four/diag/trans). The CNF builder and the RUP checker are reimplemented here.\n  - (I3) and (I4), plus gluing, on the complete classes: 24 and 22 of them.\n  - Lemma 9 witness connectivity for every line of an incomplete class: 6 and 14 lines, all six column pairs witnessed.\n- **Proof:** #1399's Step 1 (#1212 Lemmas 5\u20136 on the complete classes), then Lemma 9 on the rest, then #1212 \u00a77.\n\n**Consequence.** With #1419, **every P110 unit** (P112 minus any two lines) is rigid. Every decoder with exactly eight costly terms in the E-graph model there has cst \u2265 62, which is #968's 72 \u2212 p at p = 10.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `python3 -I -B research/complex-rank8-rigidity-p110-odd/verify.py` runs 26 exact checks in about 2 s, standard library only. It is independent of #1212's code: its own E8 model, orbits, classes, witnesses, gluing, Lemma 9 checks, CNF and two-watched-literal RUP checker. It replays the shipped proofs against CNFs it builds itself, and the SHA256 of both the proofs and the CNFs is pinned. Its controls:\n  - the gauge zero pattern satisfies the CNF without the \"some entry vanishes\" clause;\n  - the proofs fail without that clause;\n  - a bare empty-clause proof is rejected.\n- **Cross-check, run once:** #1212's own `rup_check` (head `57099cb5`) accepts both proofs on this package's CNFs, with identical lemma counts, and rejects them without the zero clause.\n- `make_proof.py` (python-sat 1.9.dev15, Glucose 4.1) regenerates the pivots and proofs in about 2 s.\n- Passes on Python 3.10, 3.12 and 3.14. `scripts/research_package.py`: the metadata check and the Python 3.12 registered replay pass. `test_research_*` passes.\n\n## Not checked or not covered\n\n- P109 and deeper punctures with an odd pair; this is the open next question. Orthogonal punctures outside a frame (see #1419's census). Nine or more costly terms.\n- #1212's Lemmas 5\u20136, \u00a77 and transport, and #1399's Lemma 9, are cited, not re-derived. Both PRs are open. #968's (F6) is inherited. Attainment of 62 is not checked. There has been no independent human review.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- **Task / scope:** `complex-masked-decoder` (scope key `2a6f2c726b78f9ae7d26`), refined to #1419's open next question. Chooser nonce `35f10aeb31e6ffea65d714368cb51223`, track complex-mechanisms, priority revision 2.\n- **Heads:** base `bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f`. Cites #1212 `57099cb5`, #1399 `4e1ba3a1`, and #1419 (orthogonal pairs only). It imports nothing from them.\n- **Claim:** https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1411 (same session as #1419).\n- **Overlap:** none on odd-pair P110 or on P109. Refreshed at 00:41Z (788 open PRs and 146 discussions, complete pagination).\n\n## Credit\n\n- **burntout76 / Brett Halligan (#1212):** the theorem, (E), the CNF families of Lemmas 4/8, the pivot reduction, Lemmas 5\u20136, \u00a77 and the transport.\n- **themilkman216 (#968):** the floor.\n- **DreamingOfClouds (#717):** the E-graph model.\n\nSubstantial AI assistance: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code (proof, verifier, CNF/RUP reimplementation, write-up). Submitted by the account holder. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
